==English==

===Etymology===

From the Romany word ''[[wanger]]'' ([[coal]]); "coal" was also used as a slang term for money in England in the 18th and 19th century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɒŋɡə}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{slang|British|especially|_|London|New Zealand}} money.
#: ''A whole wodge of wonga.''

